---
// /brands/lacanche-range-repair/ — Luxury Wave L-3. Lacanche (Burgundy, France).
// French made-to-order range cookers, ALL-ANALOG (mechanical thermostats/valves) — the
// serviceability differentiator. US importer/exclusive distributor Art Culinaire
// (frenchranges.com), LA showroom, NA parts stock. Model lines named after Burgundy towns
// (Cluny/Volnay/Beaune/Sully). NO sourced failure pattern — frame around wear items +
// calibration, never invent a defect. $89 residential. Verified: Art Culinaire + brand.
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ServiceHero from '../../components/ServiceHero.astro';
import BrandBranchesGrid from '../../components/BrandBranchesGrid.astro';
import { MAIN_PHONE, MAIN_PHONE_TEL } from '../../data/branches';
import { mergeCredentials } from '../../data/credentials-schema';
import { BRANCH_LOCATIONS_GEO_NEUTRAL } from '../../lib/build-location-array';
import { OPENING_HOURS_SCHEMA } from '../../data/business-hours';

const title = "Lacanche Range Repair Los Angeles — Same Day";
const description = "Lacanche French range repair across LA and the Westside. All-analog Cluny, Volnay, Beaune, and Sully ranges — igniters, thermocouples, valves, calibration. Art Culinaire parts. $89 diagnostic.";
const canonical = "https://samedayappliance.repair/brands/lacanche-range-repair/";

const faqs = [
  { q: "Can you actually get parts for a French Lacanche range in LA?", a: "Yes — and better than most people expect for a French range. Lacanche's exclusive US distributor is Art Culinaire (they've imported the brand since 1995 and run a showroom in Los Angeles), and they hold North American parts stock rather than single-sourcing every part from Burgundy. The wear parts our techs actually replace on a Lacanche — igniters, thermocouples, gas valves, oven thermostats, door hinges and gaskets — are the ones Art Culinaire keeps available, typically shipping in a day or two. That's the practical difference between a Lacanche and a bespoke French range where every part is a special order: on a Lacanche, the everyday service items are genuinely obtainable. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair." },
  { q: "Is a Lacanche easier to repair than an electronic luxury range?", a: "In our experience, yes, and it's the brand's quiet advantage. A Lacanche is essentially all-analog — mechanical thermostats, mechanical gas valves, standing pilots or spark igniters, no proprietary control board running the oven. That matters two ways. First, there's no expensive electronic board to fail or to source from France; the things that wear are mechanical and rebuildable. Second, a technician who understands gas cooking can diagnose a Lacanche by testing the flame, the thermocouple signal, and the valve directly, rather than chasing a fault code. So while a Lacanche is a serious, heavy piece of equipment, the actual repair is often more straightforward than on a computerized range of similar price." },
  { q: "Which Lacanche models do you service?", a: "All of them — the line is named after Burgundy towns and sized by width. The Cluny (about 39 inches, the entry into the range) is the most common in LA kitchens; from there the Volnay, Beaune, and the larger multi-oven Sully and Fontenay run up through the wide Cormatin, Vougeot, Chagny, Chassagne, and Saulieu. Whatever the width or the cooktop configuration you specced — burners, the French plaque simmer plate, a plancha, or a wok ring — our techs service the burners, ovens, and the analog controls the same way. Tell us the model name when you call and we'll bring the wear parts most likely to fit." },
  { q: "My Lacanche oven isn't holding temperature — what's wrong?", a: "On an analog range like a Lacanche, an oven that runs hot, runs cold, or drifts is almost always the mechanical oven thermostat or a calibration issue rather than a failed circuit board — because there isn't one. Our techs put a calibrated thermometer in the cavity, compare it against the dial across the range, and either recalibrate the thermostat or replace it if it's out of spec. On the gas ovens we also check the thermocouple and the safety valve, since a weak thermocouple can make the oven cut out or under-fire. It's a classic wear-and-calibration fix, not a diagnostic mystery. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair." },
  { q: "Is a Lacanche always worth repairing?", a: "Almost always. A Lacanche is a made-to-order, hand-assembled range built in Burgundy — often a $15,000 to $40,000-plus centerpiece of an estate kitchen in Beverly Hills, Bel Air, or Malibu — and it's engineered to be a lifetime appliance. Because the design is analog and mechanical, the parts that wear are serviceable and available through Art Culinaire, so there's rarely a scenario where the range is 'totaled' by a repair. Even a burner assembly, a full valve service, or an oven rebuild is a fraction of replacement, and the range keeps its value. We'll always give you the honest number, but on a Lacanche the answer is nearly always repair." },
  { q: "Do you service the Lacanche's specialty cooktop pieces — the plaque, plancha, or wok ring?", a: "Yes. Part of what people buy a Lacanche for is the configurable top: the French plaque (a solid simmer/heat-storage plate), a plancha, a wok ring, or a mix of open burners. Those are mechanical assemblies fed by the same gas valves and igniters as the standard burners, so our techs service them the same way — checking the valve, the igniter, the flame, and the plate's heat distribution. If a plaque is heating unevenly or a burner under a specialty grate won't light, it's the same gas-side diagnosis, just under a different top piece." },
  { q: "How fast can you get to a Lacanche on the Westside?", a: "Same-day in most cases across Los Angeles, Beverly Hills, Bel Air, Malibu, and the wider Westside, with our other branches covering Orange County, Ventura, San Bernardino, and Riverside. Lacanche owners tend to be in the estate belt, which is our densest service area, so a Lacanche call in Beverly Hills or the Palisades is usually a fast turnaround. We answer the phone 24/7 and carry the common Lacanche wear parts, so a lot of calls are one visit. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair." }
];

const schema = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@graph": [
  { "@type": "Service", "serviceType": "Lacanche Range Repair", "provider": { "@id": canonical + "#org" }, "areaServed": [
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Los Angeles County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Orange County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Ventura County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Santa Barbara County" }, { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "San Bernardino County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Riverside County" }, { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "San Diego County" }
    ], "description": "Lacanche French range repair across Los Angeles and the Westside. All-analog Cluny, Volnay, Beaune, Sully, and Fontenay ranges — igniters, thermocouples, gas valves, oven thermostats, calibration, hinges, and specialty cooktop pieces. Parts through US distributor Art Culinaire. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair." },
  { "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": faqs.map(f => ({ "@type": "Question", "name": f.q, "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": f.a.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, '') } })) },
  { "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [ { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://samedayappliance.repair/" }, { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Brands", "item": "https://samedayappliance.repair/brands/" }, { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Lacanche Range Repair", "item": canonical } ] }
] };

const wave46OrgSchema = mergeCredentials({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HomeAndConstructionBusiness',
  '@id': canonical + '#org',
  name: 'Same Day Appliance Repair',
  url: canonical,
  priceRange: '$$',
  openingHoursSpecification: OPENING_HOURS_SCHEMA,
  areaServed: [
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Los Angeles County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Orange County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Ventura County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Santa Barbara County' }, { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'San Bernardino County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Riverside County' }, { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'San Diego County' }
  ],
  location: BRANCH_LOCATIONS_GEO_NEUTRAL
});
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <Fragment slot="head-scripts">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(wave46OrgSchema)} />
  </Fragment>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
  <div class="call-banner"><div class="wrap"><span>Lacanche needs service? Same-day on the Westside:</span><a href={`tel:${MAIN_PHONE_TEL}`} class="phone-lg">{MAIN_PHONE}</a></div></div>
  <ServiceHero
    section="brands"
    slug="lacanche-range-repair"
    eyebrow={"Lacanche Range Repair"}
    title={"Lacanche Range Repair, Los Angeles & the Westside"}
    subtitle={description}
    heroImageTitle={"Lacanche French Range Repair"}
  />

  <BrandBranchesGrid />
  <section class="trust-bar"><div class="wrap"><span>Licensed BHGS #A49573 · Insured</span><span>Same-day · 7 Southern California counties</span><span>$89 residential diagnostic · waived with repair</span></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>Lacanche, the French range that's actually built to be repaired</h2>
    <p>A Lacanche is one of the few luxury ranges where our first reaction on the service call is relief rather than concern. It's made to order in the village of Lacanche in Burgundy, hand-assembled, and — this is the part that matters for repair — it's essentially all-analog. Mechanical oven thermostats, mechanical gas valves, standing pilots or simple spark igniters, and no proprietary control board running the cooking. When a Lacanche acts up in a Beverly Hills or Bel Air kitchen, there's no fault code to chase and no French circuit board to wait on; our techs test the flame, the thermocouple, and the valve directly and fix the mechanical part that's worn. The failures are wear items — an igniter, a thermocouple, a gas valve, an oven thermostat drifting out of calibration, a door hinge or gasket — and every one of them is serviceable. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair, BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410).</p>
    <p>Because there's no computer between you and the burners, a Lacanche ages gracefully. The same range that a Malibu estate installed a decade ago is still the same range mechanically, and the parts that wear are the parts a technician who knows gas cooking can rebuild or replace. That's the quiet advantage over the electronic pro-ranges in the same price bracket: fewer failure points, and the ones that exist are honest mechanical ones. Our techs treat a Lacanche the way it's meant to be treated — as a lifetime appliance that needs periodic wear service and calibration, not a disposable that gets replaced when a board dies.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>Getting Lacanche parts in LA — the Art Culinaire pipeline</h2>
    <p>The parts question is the one that scares people off French ranges, and on a Lacanche the answer is genuinely reassuring. Lacanche's exclusive US distributor is Art Culinaire, which has imported the brand since 1995 and runs a Los Angeles showroom. Crucially, Art Culinaire holds North American parts stock and runs a nationwide network of preferred service providers, so the everyday Lacanche wear parts — igniters, thermocouples, gas valves, oven thermostats, hinges, gaskets — are available in North America and typically ship in a day or two rather than crossing the Atlantic on a special order.</p>
    <p>That's the practical line between a Lacanche and a truly bespoke French range like a La Cornue Château, where the most specialized parts are special-order from France with real lead time. On a Lacanche, the mechanical service items are the obtainable ones. Our techs keep the common Lacanche wear parts on the van where we can, and source the rest through the North American channel — so a Lacanche repair in Los Angeles is usually a matter of days, not months. When a part genuinely has to come from Burgundy, we'll tell you that up front and give you the timeline honestly.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap">
    <h2>Lacanche ranges we service</h2>
    <div class="model-grid">
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Cluny (~39")</h3><p>The entry Lacanche and the most common in LA kitchens — a single-oven range with a configurable cooktop. Service: burner igniters, thermocouples, gas valves, oven thermostat calibration, door hinge and gasket.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Volnay & Beaune</h3><p>Mid-width ranges stepping up in cooktop and oven capacity. Same all-analog controls; same wear-item service on burners, ovens, and valves.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Sully & Fontenay</h3><p>The larger multi-oven Lacanche ranges — a second oven (often electric alongside the gas) means a second thermostat and heating circuit our techs check and calibrate. Estate-kitchen centerpieces in Bel Air and the Palisades.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Cormatin, Vougeot, Chagny, Chassagne, Saulieu</h3><p>The wide, multi-oven flagship Lacanche ranges. More burners, more ovens, more specialty top pieces — all fed by the same serviceable analog valves and igniters.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Specialty cooktop pieces</h3><p>The French plaque (solid simmer plate), plancha, and wok ring that make a Lacanche configurable. Fed by the same gas valves and igniters, serviced the same way — flame, valve, igniter, heat distribution.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Matching Lacanche hoods</h3><p>The ventilation Lacanche offers to match the range. Fan motor, switch, and lighting service where the hood is part of the installation.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>What Lacanche service looks like — and what it costs</h2>
    <p>$89 flat residential diagnostic, waived with repair. Because a Lacanche has no control board, the work is honest gas-and-mechanical service. Typical wear-item ranges our techs see:</p>
    <table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Typical range (parts + labor)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Oven thermostat recalibration</td><td>$140–$260</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Thermocouple replacement</td><td>$180–$340</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Burner igniter / spark module</td><td>$200–$400</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Oven thermostat replacement</td><td>$260–$480</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Gas valve replacement</td><td>$300–$560</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Door hinge / gasket service</td><td>$220–$440</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Full burner assembly service</td><td>$300–$600</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p class="small">Ranges are typical and depend on the model and how many burners or ovens are involved; a specialty part sourced through Art Culinaire's North American channel can shift a specific line. There's no proprietary board on a Lacanche, so you won't see the $800–$1,200 board-replacement line that computerized luxury ranges carry — one more reason a Lacanche stays worth repairing.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>Related luxury range pages</h2>
    <ul class="related-links">
      <li><a href="/brands/la-cornue-range-repair/">La Cornue range repair Los Angeles</a> — the bespoke French range (Château &amp; CornuFé)</li>
      <li><a href="/brands/officine-gullo-range-repair/">Officine Gullo range repair Los Angeles</a> — hand-built Florentine ranges</li>
      <li><a href="/brands/wolf-range-repair/">Wolf range repair Los Angeles</a> — the American pro-range benchmark</li>
      <li><a href="/brands/aga-stove-repair/">AGA cooker repair Los Angeles</a> — British cast-iron heat-storage</li>
      <li><a href="/services/oven-repair/">All oven &amp; range repair in Los Angeles →</a></li>
      <li><a href="/beverly-hills/">Beverly Hills service area</a> · <a href="/malibu/">Malibu service area</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap narrow"><h2>Lacanche repair, frequently asked</h2>{faqs.map(f => <details class="faq"><summary>{f.q}</summary><p set:html={f.a}></p></details>)}</div></section>

  <section id="book" class="cta-bottom"><div class="wrap"><h2>Lacanche need service? Call the branch nearest your kitchen.</h2><p>Same-day across LA, the Westside, Orange County, Ventura, San Bernardino, and Riverside. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair.</p></div></section>
</Layout>

<style>
  body { color: var(--text); } .wrap { max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; } .wrap.narrow { max-width: 820px; }
  h1 { font-size: 2.4rem; line-height: 1.15; margin: 12px 0 20px; color: var(--black); } h2 { font-size: 1.8rem; margin: 0 0 16px; color: var(--black); } h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 0 0 10px; color: var(--black); } p { line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .call-banner { background: var(--red); color: #fff; padding: 10px 0; } .call-banner .wrap { display:flex; gap: 14px; align-items: center; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; } .call-banner .phone-lg { color:#fff; font-weight: 800; text-decoration: underline; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .trust-bar { background: var(--red); color: #fff; padding: 14px 0; } .trust-bar .wrap { display: flex; gap: 28px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .section { padding: 56px 0; } .section.alt { background: var(--gray); }
  .model-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px; } .model-card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 20px; border-radius: 6px; }
  .price-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 14px; background: #fff; } .price-table th, .price-table td { text-align: left; padding: 11px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); } .price-table th { background: var(--black); color: #fff; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.95rem; } .small { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.92rem; margin-top: 12px; }
  .related-links { list-style: none; padding: 0; } .related-links li { padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); } .related-links a { color: var(--red); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; } .related-links a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .faq { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 8px; border-radius: 4px; } .faq summary { font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; padding: 4px 0; } .faq p { margin: 8px 0 0; }
  .cta-bottom { background: var(--black); color: #fff; padding: 48px 0; } .cta-bottom h2 { color: #fff; } .cta-bottom p { color: #c9c9c9; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; } h2 { font-size: 1.45rem; }  .trust-bar .wrap { gap: 14px; font-size: 0.85rem; } }
</style>
